JFtn follow-up work
===================

Reviewed against the source and tests on 2026-10-17.
Implemented behavior and limits are documented under docs/.

Remaining implementation
------------------------

- Implement browser netmail/echomail readers, drafts and composition.
  Administrative mail reading, drafts and submission already exist in RPC.
- Add point-scoped mailbox permissions and APIs. Approved AKA claims already exist;
  the current node-wide UiService still requires ADMIN for every operation.
- Add RPC/UI editing for netmail routing rules and safe link removal/renaming.
  Link creation/editing, separate PKT passwords and basic tosser settings already
  exist in the UI. Core/SQL routing-rule APIs are available.
- Decide whether to implement or remove the empty legacy JAMEchoBase.getMessage()
  and delMessage() methods. JamArea and the JAM bridge already support mail access.
- Add durable automatic poll retries/backoff and incoming-session tracking.
  Outgoing queue inspection, manual polling/retry, cancellation, history and
  per-attempt journals already work through RPC/UI.
- Define explicit administration of prepared outbound deliveries (for example,
  hold/release/removal), including safety while a transport owns a file.
  Outbound inspection and existing routing/Hold behavior are already implemented.
- Add safe retention/cleanup for mail delivery receipts, processing/script/JAM
  journals and received-file archives. Poll history already has count-based
  retention via PollHistoryLimit, and pruning also deletes its attempt journals.
- Expand fault-injection tests for sender deadlines, disk-full/close/fsync failures
  and crash boundaries across supported platforms. Restart/recovery, malformed
  input, connection failure and cross-process JAM locking already have tests.

Optional future scope (not committed features)
---------------------------------------------

- Select additional binkp/TIC extensions or services only with explicit protocol
  requirements and interoperability/security tests; current limits are in docs/.
- Consider a lightweight distribution without UI/RPC. The no-JRE ZIP is already
  available, but still contains the full application and is not a lightweight build.
- Consider an RSS posting robot.

Current scope and test limits:
- docs/tosser.md
- docs/rpc-ui.md
- docs/web-ui.md
- docs/test-coverage.md
